  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict all-incident reporting with 24h initial notice and 72h customer notice. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% limit but allows sales to continue above 5% with corrective action and possible regulator restriction, and requires per-model results to customers but not public publication. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 uses an 8/100k review trigger rather than mandatory recall, with recall or corrective action upon review."
